## HTTP Exception Rule

Raw HTTP (`HttpClient` / `IHttpClientFactory`) is allowed **ONLY** when ECCore gateway is not applicable:
- External third-party / vendor APIs
- Internal tools not in ECCore gateway (e.g. GitLab, Confluence)
- Requests requiring `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, multipart, streaming, or custom auth not supported by ECCore

**When using raw HTTP:**
- MUST add a comment explaining why ECCore cannot be used
- MUST isolate implementation in Infrastructure / Provider layer
- MUST NOT call raw HTTP from Controller or Service layer
- MUST NOT introduce new third-party HTTP libraries
- SHOULD prefer built-in `HttpClient` / `IHttpClientFactory`
- SHOULD wrap behind a project interface

```csharp
// Correct — raw HTTP wrapped in Infrastructure, reason documented
public interface IConfluenceProvider
{
    Task CreatePageAsync(CreateConfluencePageRequest request);
}

// Implementation in Infrastructure — comment explains ECCore exception
[DependencyInjection(typeof(IConfluenceProvider))]
public class ConfluenceProvider : IConfluenceProvider
{
    // ECCore gateway does not support Confluence; using HttpClient directly
    private readonly HttpClient _http;
    ...
}
```

